\newlabel{tab:seg-const}{{26}{97}{Constants of the minor operations of each stage of the segmentation block, with the reason for each. Every entry in units of the measured pitch $P$ scales with the page; the four that do not are the Otsu range, the $0.2\,\%$ and $0.45$ paper-region tests and the floor of 60 ink pixels. The constants of the core operations appear in the equations of Section~\ref {sec:segmentation} itself}{table.caption.83}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {27}{\ignorespaces The eight discard predicates applied to each closed piece of ink in stage~4; the background label is exempt from all of them. The first row is the most aggressive rule in the module: any piece whose leftmost ink lies within $e$ of the left frame edge is discarded whatever its size or darkness, which removes the facing page of an open book but also costs the first letters of a page photographed with no left margin.}}{98}{table.caption.85}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:seg-artifact}{{27}{98}{The eight discard predicates applied to each closed piece of ink in stage~4; the background label is exempt from all of them. The first row is the most aggressive rule in the module: any piece whose leftmost ink lies within $e$ of the left frame edge is discarded whatever its size or darkness, which removes the facing page of an open book but also costs the first letters of a page photographed with no left margin}{table.caption.85}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces The pixel-ownership correction rules of stage~6. The size ladder they share runs $0.006P^2$, $0.01P^2$, $0.015P^2$, $0.03P^2$, $0.05P^2$, $0.065P^2$, $0.1P^2$, $0.12P^2$ and $0.2P^2$, every entry a multiple of the measured pitch squared, so no rule is tied to a pixel count.}}{98}{table.caption.87}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:seg-own}{{28}{98}{The pixel-ownership correction rules of stage~6. The size ladder they share runs $0.006P^2$, $0.01P^2$, $0.015P^2$, $0.03P^2$, $0.05P^2$, $0.065P^2$, $0.1P^2$, $0.12P^2$ and $0.2P^2$, every entry a multiple of the measured pitch squared, so no rule is tied to a pixel count}{table.caption.87}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsubsection}{Pseudocode of the four routines that carry the arithmetic}{98}{subsubsection*.88}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {36}{\ignorespaces The three array primitives of the segmentation block as pseudocode. \texttt  {BoxMean} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-sat}, \texttt  {AnyWithinRadius} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-dilate} and \texttt  {LongRunMask} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-runmask}. Because each is built on a cumulative sum, a window of any size costs four look-ups, which is what makes the 40-pixel illumination blur of stage~2 affordable.}}{99}{figure.caption.89}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seg-primspseudo}{{36}{99}{The three array primitives of the segmentation block as pseudocode. \texttt {BoxMean} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-sat}, \texttt {AnyWithinRadius} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-dilate} and \texttt {LongRunMask} is Equation~\ref {eq:seg-runmask}. Because each is built on a cumulative sum, a window of any size costs four look-ups, which is what makes the 40-pixel illumination blur of stage~2 affordable}{figure.caption.89}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces Lighting normalisation and the ink mask as pseudocode. The array \texttt  {ratio} is $\rho $ of Equation~\ref {eq:seg-flat} and \texttt  {OtsuThreshold} is the cumulative form of Equation~\ref {eq:seg-otsu} evaluated for all 256 bins at once. The threshold 0.999 rather than 1 absorbs floating-point error in the integral image; no pen stroke fills a $9\times 9$ window, so a window that is wholly ink is a shadow or a binder and is removed with its fringe.}}{99}{figure.caption.90}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seg-inkpseudo}{{37}{99}{Lighting normalisation and the ink mask as pseudocode. The array \texttt {ratio} is $\rho $ of Equation~\ref {eq:seg-flat} and \texttt {OtsuThreshold} is the cumulative form of Equation~\ref {eq:seg-otsu} evaluated for all 256 bins at once. The threshold 0.999 rather than 1 absorbs floating-point error in the integral image; no pen stroke fills a $9\times 9$ window, so a window that is wholly ink is a shadow or a binder and is removed with its fringe}{figure.caption.90}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{Supporting detail of the text recogniser}{99}{subsection*.93}\protected@file@percent }
